PLAN = BASE_PLAN + ''' Missing optional libraries alone do not establish a missing prerequisite: an available package manager may install them, and standard-library inspection may still produce useful observations. Prefer a task-relevant reusable preparation over merely reporting an already-observed absence. For structured input files, a standard-library inventory of actual section/column names, counts, and format anomalies is a safe input_schema_check; preserve its compact output in a file. This must not compute specialist answers, interpret figures, or copy whole input files into model context. Choose report_missing_evidence only for a concrete prerequisite that cannot be inspected or prepared from the supplied task and environment. Do not invent an unavailable network or installation restriction.'''

OBSERVATIONS = ''' Treat context and tool output as a cost. Never dump entire datasets or concatenate multiple large input files into the conversation. Inspect a small representative header/schema first, then read only the sections needed for the current question. Perform numerical/data processing in programs over the original complete files; print concise summaries, exact errors, and requirement-check results. Redirect verbose diagnostics to a named file in /app and inspect relevant ranges when needed. For shell tools request max_output_tokens around 1500; retained tool output has a 2048-token target. A truncated observation is incomplete evidence, not success: obtain a focused follow-up if necessary. Keep full data and code on disk. Use distinctive helper filenames that do not shadow standard-library modules. These limits concern observations only; do not drop required calculations or substitute guessed outputs.'''
ADVISOR = BASE_ADVISOR + OBSERVATIONS
SOL_ADVISOR = BASE_SOL_ADVISOR + OBSERVATIONS
DECISION = BASE_DECISION + ''' Workspace excerpts may contain metadata or explicitly truncated previews rather than entire artifact serializations. Neither file existence, a hash, size, nor a truncated preview proves correctness. Assess the actual execution and original-requirement checks. If evidence is insufficient, request one focused read or executable requirement check through the worker/advisor; do not accept an artifact solely because it exists.'''
